Package: MCMCGraph
Title: Bayesian MCMC Functional Clustering for Paired Longitudinal Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Ruiqi", "Zhao", email = "karongzrq@163.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Author: Ruiqi Zhao [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Ruiqi Zhao <karongzrq@163.com>
Description: Bayesian finite mixture clustering of paired (K = 2) longitudinal
    trajectories. Each feature carries two individuals' time courses that are
    clustered jointly through a shared cluster label and a cluster-specific
    paired Legendre-polynomial mean curve. Within-individual residual
    correlation is modelled by a structured antedependence (SAD) covariance
    with a single shared time-correlation parameter. Inference is run with the
    'nimble' MCMC engine (Gibbs plus slice samplers), and label switching is
    resolved by an ECR-style relabeling step before posterior summaries and BIC
    model selection.
